<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Markets quiet, rain forecast.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Markets quiet, rain forecast.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wheat sales were light in the central and southern Great Plains hard red winter wheat markets with farmers reluctant to increase to new-crop sales because of freeze damage and dry conditions, dealers said.</p>
<p>No rain fell in dry northwest Kansas this week but dealers there said forecasts called for a good chance of rain Thursday or Thursday night. Much of southern and western Kansas was overcast early Thursday with rain likely.</p>
<p>Oklahoma said wheat was developing well and most had headed. However, more rain would aid development, dealers there said.</p>
<p>Higher wheat basis bids this week at the U.S. Gulf kept most interior basis bids firm.</p>
